#: ../../topics/domains.rst:14
msgid "**JavaScript domain** (``js``): JavaScript functions, methods, classes, and properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:15
msgid "**Odin domain** (``odin``): Native Odin packages, procedures, structs, unions, and enums (see :doc:`../odin`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:16
msgid "**Rust domain** (``rust``): Rust crates, modules, functions, structs, enums, traits, impls, and macros (see `Rust domain`_ below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:18
msgid "Setting the primary domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:21
msgid "The default domain is set with ``primary_domain`` in ``conf.toml`` (default: ``\"py\"``). When a primary domain is active, its directives and roles can be written without the domain prefix (for example, ``.. function::`` instead of ``.. py:function::``, and ``:func:`name``` instead of ``:py:func:`name```)."
