msgid "Cross-referencing conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:287
msgid "Cross-references in domains support several modifiers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:289
msgid "**Hide prefix**: Prefixing the target with a tilde (``~``) displays only the final component of the target name. For example, ``:py:func:`~pipeline.reader.DocumentReader.parse``` renders as ``parse()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:290
msgid "**Current scope resolution**: Relative references look up names within the active module or namespace before falling back to global lookup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:291
msgid "**Exact match**: Prefixing with a dot (``.``) searches from the current module or enclosing object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:293
msgid "The Rust domain follows the same conventions with ``::`` paths: ``:rust:struct:`~my_crate::geometry::Point``` renders as ``Point``."
msgstr ""

